Package: mixeff
Title: Mixed-Effects Models via the 'mixeff-rs' Rust Crate
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Brad", "Buchsbaum",
           email = "bbuchsbaum@research.baycrest.org",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = "author of mixeff and the bundled 'mixeff-rs' crate"),
    person("Authors of the dependency Rust crates",
           role = "ctb",
           comment = "see inst/AUTHORS for details"))
Copyright: file inst/COPYRIGHTS
Description: Fits linear and generalized linear mixed-effects models
    from 'lme4'-style formulas, with optimization by the bundled
    'mixeff-rs' Rust crate. A fitted model stores the compiled model
    specification, the optimizer certificate, and per-coefficient
    inference metadata (method, status, reliability) as data, so a result
    can be inspected, saved, and reloaded without a live handle to the
    compiled engine. When an inference method is unavailable for a fit,
    the affected value is either withheld with a stable reason code or
    reported under the name of the method actually used, never silently
    swapped. Vignettes cover migration from 'lme4' and the meaning of
    random-effects formula syntax.
